/** CPE-49 strong-retrofit batch 6 (upgrade to the 4-case standard: Sample + boundary + tricky +
 * stress). Boundary cases are the exact ones from the original seed-cpe49-batch6.ts, re-verified
 * against freshly written reference solutions before trusting them for new tricky/stress. This
 * batch's original boundary cases were mostly degenerate edge inputs (e.g. "0 0 min" for
 * satellites, n=1 for the median problem) that don't exercise the real formulas at all, so
 * wherever this project's own scraped Sample had a richer multi-case dataset beyond the boundary,
 * it was used as an extra verification pass before trusting a new solution -- and it caught two
 * real bugs this round:
 *
 * - uva-10242-fourth-point: the original assumption (p2 always the shared vertex, fourth =
 *   p1+p4-p2) matched the boundary but FAILED against 5 of the 16 lines in the real official
 *   sample, which also share the vertex via p1==p3, p1==p4, or p2==p4 depending on the line.
 *   Rewritten to detect which pair of the four given points actually coincides before computing
 *   the fourth point, verified against the full sample.
 * - uva-10908-largest-squares: no new bug, but this pass independently re-verified all 4 of the
 *   original boundary's (r,c) queries (3, 1, 5, 1) against a freshly written brute-force solution
 *   rather than trusting the stored numbers alone.
 *
 * Other verifications against real official samples (not just the boundary) this pass:
 * - uva-10221-satellites: all 16 lines of the real sample (arc = R*angle_rad, chord =
 *   2*R*sin(angle_rad/2), R = 6440+altitude, minutes converted to degrees /60).
 * - uva-10057-a-mid-summer-night-s-dream: median-based min-sum-of-abs-deviations, matched the
 *   sample's 2-case output including the odd-n unique-median path.
 * - uva-299-train-swapping: merge-sort inversion count, matched all 25 cases of the real sample
 *   (also fixed a crash on the sample's own leading CRLF-scraping blank line).
 * - uva-10226-hardwood-species and uva-10062-tell-me-the-frequencies: both matched their real
 *   multi-case samples byte-for-byte on the first attempt, confirming the "blank line between
 *   cases" formatting in both problems' actual expected output (unlike uva-11005 in batch 5,
 *   where that same phrasing in the spec turned out to NOT match the real judge).
 *
 * tricky cases: uva-10057 an even-n wide-median-range case; uva-10221 a 90-degree and a
 * full-circle-in-minutes case; uva-10642 two general (non-boundary-corner) source/destination
 * pairs; uva-10242 the p1==p3 sharing pattern specifically; uva-10062 a 3-way frequency tie
 * (descending-ASCII tiebreak); uva-10908 a query at the exact grid corner (forced side=1);
 * uva-299 an already-sorted (0 swaps) and a fully-reversed (maximum swaps) permutation;
 * uva-10226 a 2-species non-trivial split plus a second single-species case (also exercises the
 * inter-case blank line).
 */
